agged the last log index (8302) because the leader stages the pre-dispatch commit index.\\\")\nnew_lim=(\\\"The seeded cases supply the commit-tracking store state directly. Three restarts rest on a real prefix: a \\\"\n         \\\"single-node leader (staged commit 8300, last log 8302, because the leader stages the pre-dispatch commit index) \\\"\n         \\\"and a three-voter cluster follower in both the snapshot and no-snapshot cases (staged commit 8400, last log 8402).\\\")\nnew['limitations']=[new_lim if l==old_lim else l for l in new['limitations']]\nnew['joint_history']=(new['joint_history']+\\\" Receipt f032fc49841048c9877653db9f877b27 comes from a second experiment \\\"\n  \\\"under this question rather than a revision of the first: it builds the committed prefix through a three-voter \\\"\n  \\\"cluster and restarts a follower, where the earlier experiment restarted a single-node leader or a hand-seeded store. \\\"\n  \\\"Its cases are named differently and its admissions are its own, so it is not a substitute for the earlier receipts; \\\"\n  \\\"it is cited because it exercises the same RestoreCommittedLogs replay boundary on the operational restart shape with \\\"\n  \\\"the same source-level mechanism.\\\")\njson.dump({'rationale':(\\\"Add the operational follower-restart receipt to the startup account: a real three-voter cluster \\\"\n  \\\"whose follower staged 8400 committed entries reproduced the same boundary, with the follower's own snapshot removing \\\"\n  \\\"the replay and the unsnapshotted restart blocking, so the earlier leader-only prefix limitation is replaced by a \\\"\n  \\\"statement of which restarts rest on a real prefix.\\\"),\n 'interpretations':[new]},open('draft/update.json','w'),indent=2)\nprint('written')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" 